{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRxtLgCBSHf6xriEDs85","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017rQhxanLbb3DkCSdL9Q7Pu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-2ecpv0; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))''','''        url = AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")\n        # A browser navigation cannot carry the Bearer header, so the SPA asks for\n        # the URL via fetch (JSON) and navigates itself; curl/direct callers get a 302.\n        if self.headers.get(\"Accept\", \"\").startswith(\"application/json\"):\n            return self.send_json(200, {\"url\": url})\n        self.redirect(url)''')\ns=s.replace('''\"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n                  \"scope\"''','''\"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n                  \"response_type\": \"code\", \"scope\"''')\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")''','''    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    # Intervals returns neither expires_in nor refresh_token: the token is long-lived.\n    # Only schedule expiry when the provider actually states a lifetime.\n    expires_in = int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None\n    if expires_in is None and not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no expires_in/refresh_token in response, treating token as non-expiring\")''')\ns=s.replace('\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in,','\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in if expires_in else None,')\ns=s.replace('if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:','if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] is None or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:')\ns=s.replace('expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))','expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None)')\ns=s.replace('DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\\n','')\nopen('server.py','w').write(s)\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE','ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\na=open('static/app.js').read()\na=a.replace('''<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>''','''<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>''')\na=a.replace('''    const d = document''','''    const cb = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (cb) cb.onclick = async () => {\n      try {\n        const r = await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/init\", { headers: { \"Accept\": \"application/json\" } });\n        location.href = r.url;\n      } catch (e) { root.insertAdjacentHTML(\"beforeend\", `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`); }\n    };\n    const d = document''',1)\nopen('static/app.js','w').write(a)\nE\npython3 -m py_compile server.py && git diff --stat\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Causes\n\n1. **Connect button always 401s (confirmed).** The button was a plain `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">`. A document navigation can't send the `Authorization: Bearer` header (the token lives in localStorage and is only added by the SPA's `fetch` wrapper), so `require_user()` rejected everyone. Fix: the button now calls `auth/init` through `api()` with `Accept: application/json`; the server returns `{url}` and the SPA navigates to it. (Plain callers still get the 302.)\n\n2. **Intervals rejects the authorize URL with `400 invalid_request` (partly unverified).** Since the calendar sync (2026-10-02) the request asks for `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`, and it also never sent `response_type=code`. Intervals' error body doesn't name the parameter, and I couldn't reach their OAuth docs, so I can't prove which one it minds. Changes: added `response_type=code`, and trimmed scopes to `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` (Rivera's working token shows WRITE was granted without a separate READ, so the READ entries look redundant). **Please test against real Intervals**; if it still 400s, bisect by removing the calendar scope first.\n\n3. **Connections \"expire\" after an hour (confirmed from log).** Intervals' token response has no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token`, i.e. the token is long-lived. `store_connection` invented a 3600s TTL (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`), and the refresher then marked the connection \"expired, reconnect\" because there was no refresh token. Fix: with no stated lifetime, `expires_at` is `None` and the refresher skips it; expiry/refresh only applies when the provider supplies `expires_in`.\n\nRivera should reconnect once after the fix (the stored connection is already expired).\nNot tested end-to-end: no access to the real Intervals service.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":29964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb4e895f-7112-456f-a00d-76dda8e96b4a","uuid":"e0454137-1b90-44b4-a27d-e6919f642366","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:37:17.856Z","request_id":"req_011CgRxtLSoJ2rwKtaptWpL7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017rQhxanLbb3DkCSdL9Q7Pu":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-2ecpv0; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''        